        "address": "40 03 03",
        "type": "01 70",
        "routed_through_the_effect": true,
        "waited_before_the_first_take_s": 30.0,
        "which_settings_and_why": "Every setting of the sweep beside this whose takes spread by more than 0.05 dB, which is the coarsest its settled settings spread by and the same figure the band reading keeps a band by. The rule reads the takes' disagreement with each other, not the reading's disagreement with anything, so which settings are here does not depend on what the answer turned out to be. Read over every take rather than over the last two: a setting whose last two agree can still have a first take the band reading throws the whole setting away for, and eleven of them did.",
        "why_the_wait": "This type glides to the placement its byte names, and at these settings it goes past the placement and comes back, which takes longer than the glide at settings further from the centre. At the worst of them the sweep's take struck at 19.6 s was already within 0.03 dB, so thirty seconds is past arrival with room. The first take is still the witness: if it disagrees with the two after it the wait is still short, and these takes say so rather than a note claiming otherwise.",
        "what_this_does_not_replace": "The sweep beside this. That run stands as what a ten-second wait measures on this type, witness takes included; this one does not write into its directories and does not resume onto its takes.",
        "loaded_once_per_setting": "The block was written and read back once per setting, not once per take, so the repeats say how well a take repeats rather than how well a write does."
      },
